title: Soul Winning – He That Winneth Souls Is Wise
description: Preaching the gospel to every creature: the harvest is plentiful, saved men sent to save men, whosoever will may come, not ashamed of the gospel, soul winning as soul warning, and going door to door with the King James Bible, from the teachings on soul winning.
output: lessons/doctrine/topic-soulwinning.html

# One deck for the whole of studies/data/topics/soulwinning.json, each theme given the same weight.
# Slide text is the author's own sentences, trimmed. The verses the teachings typed out are shown from the KJV.
# Fixed: "our only purpose" for "out only purpose" (16326), "greet a scoffer" for "great a scoffer" (17386).

=== Introduction
--- Soul Winning [title]
overline: Doctrine · Soul winning
heading: He That Winneth Souls Is Wise
sub: Preaching the gospel to every creature.
refs: Proverbs 11:30; Mark 16:15; Romans 10:14-15; Luke 10:2
hint: Use the arrow keys or swipe to move. Tap any gold reference to read the verse.

# from 13892, 17190
--- Saved to save people
big: Proverbs 11:30 | mark: he that winneth souls is wise
lead: “Fruit” in the Biblical sense, means people who've been led to the Lord. Those saved by hearing the gospel from someone else who is saved.
p: It doesn't mean doing good works or following the commandments. We do good works and follow the commandments so that we may bear more fruit.
take: This is our calling. We are saved to save people.

=== The harvest is plentiful
# from 9333, 9335
--- The labourers are few
kicker: The harvest is plentiful
big: Luke 10:2 | mark: The harvest truly is great, but the labourers are few
p: Jesus says that while the harvest is great, there are too few laborers to bring it all in. This remains true, especially today.
p: If you aren't in a position to go out yourself, pray that you can be. Work towards it. But pray without ceasing for those who are, and that more may come. If Jesus tells us to pray, then pray.

# from 1475, 2032
--- One soweth, another reapeth
kicker: The harvest is plentiful
scripture: John 4:35-37 | mark: they are white already to harvest; One soweth, and another reapeth
p: In our labors for Christ, some of us will sow seeds and never see if they germinate and grow to fruit ripe for harvesting. Some of us water the seeds sown by others. Some are blessed to reap. All will rejoice in Heaven when we meet those we've helped win to the Lord.
p: The fruit we bear are converted and saved Christians, who like a branch of a vine then produce more fruit, and so on. One long vine back to Him, the true vine ([[John 15:5]]).

# from 9333, 12549
--- Two by two
kicker: The harvest is plentiful
big: Luke 10:1 | mark: sent them two and two before his face
p: We note the pattern of evangelism given throughout the new testament. Going forth in pairs, taking with them no provision other than what they carried on their backs, and the word of God. Preaching that the Kingdom of God is nigh.
p: And the message to the soul winners to be of good courage remains true. Like the twelve spies sent to bring of the fruit of the land, the first ripe grapes ([[Numbers 13:20]]).

# from 15975, 9286
--- The Christian's mission statement
kicker: The harvest is plentiful
scripture: Luke 4:18-19 | mark: he hath anointed me to preach the gospel to the poor
p: Not only does this proclamation give witness to His ministry, but it also serves as a mission statement for all Christians. In Him, we are filled with the Spirit. We are anointed Priests of the Lord. We are His Ministers, in Christ.
p: Do we do everything in our meager power to show compassion on the spiritually sick that they may be healed? The best of us fall short. Most of us don't really even try.
