=== Whosoever will may come
# from 10873
--- The word is nigh thee
kicker: Whosoever will may come
scripture: Romans 10:9-13 | mark: For whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved
p: That's the simplicity of the Gospel. There are no works, no special status, no secret traditions, ordinances, sacraments or other deeds of the law. And knowing this, then we must preach this glad tiding, that others may by the power of God's word, hear, believe and confess unto salvation.

# from 11308
--- The Romans Road
kicker: Whosoever will may come
p: A short but direct use of scripture, used by evangelists to win souls to the Lord for generations.
xr: John 3:16 | God so loved the world
xr: Romans 3:23 | All have sinned, and come short of the glory of God
xr: Romans 6:23 | The wages of sin is death; but the gift of God is eternal life
xr: Romans 5:8 | While we were yet sinners, Christ died for us
xr: Romans 10:9-10 | Confess with thy mouth, believe in thine heart
xr: Romans 10:13 | Whosoever shall call upon the name of the Lord shall be saved
p: It is not the only means of giving the Gospel, but it is one of the most effective. It covers all the bases.

# from 17283, 17705
--- At the door
kicker: Whosoever will may come
panel: “I'm a good person” | Most experienced soulwinners will turn to Revelation 21:8, and highlight “all liars,” making the sincere appeal, “We have all told lies.” This will often break the impasse. [[Revelation 21:8]] [[Proverbs 24:9]]
panel: “Have you ever cried out to the Lord for help?” | Nearly all will say “Yes” if they're being honest. From there, it becomes easier to lead them to the truth that they need to call upon the name of the Lord specifically to save them, eternally. [[Psalm 12:1]]
p: Some will pushback to any gospel presentation with scorn. We shake the dust and move on ([[Luke 9:5]]).

# from 6080, 15232, 17180
--- Compel them to come in
kicker: Whosoever will may come
big: Luke 14:23 | mark: Go out into the highways and hedges, and compel them to come in
p: Just as with Hezekiah's letters to all Israel, many made excuses, or mocked the invitation. But many were compelled to come, turning their heart to the Lord. Both bad and good.
p: The leper believes, and calls upon Jesus to heal him, and Jesus, moved with compassion does so. *If thou wilt, thou canst make me clean* ([[Mark 1:40-41]]).

--- Compel them to come in, continued
kicker: Whosoever will may come
big: Revelation 22:17 | mark: whosoever will, let him take the water of life freely
