=== Not ashamed of the gospel
# from 11931, 10668
--- The power of God unto salvation
kicker: Not ashamed of the gospel
big: Romans 1:16 | mark: For I am not ashamed of the gospel of Christ: for it is the power of God unto salvation
p: When we share the Gospel to others, we are an instrument that reveals the nature of God to others. His righteousness. We cannot be afraid to share the good news. We can't hide our light under a bushel.

# from 10874, 11406
--- The power is in the word
kicker: Not ashamed of the gospel
big: Romans 10:17 | mark: faith cometh by hearing, and hearing by the word of God
p: The power to save men's souls is in God's word. Not our logical arguments, not in our boasts or testimonials. But by scripture.
p: You see Philip with the eunuch expounds on who Christ is from scripture. When Paul and Silas were with the Philippian jailer, *they spake unto him the word of the Lord* ([[Acts 16:31-32]]). The scriptures are a rock. They do not change.

# from 16119, 16325, 16326
--- Soul winning is soul warning
kicker: Not ashamed of the gospel
scripture: Ezekiel 33:6 | mark: his blood will I require at the watchman’s hand
p: Only the person you're warning can take the gospel you give them, the Spirit working on them, and believe. But we can and must warn them.
p: If you passed the home of strangers, and saw a fire spreading, wouldn't you bang on the door to get them to evacuate? Or would you pass on by, leaving them to burn?
big: Acts 20:26 | mark: I am pure from the blood of all men

# from 9945, 15478, 17780
--- Excuses
kicker: Not ashamed of the gospel
lead: For many of us, for much of our lives, we are like Moses. We have every excuse in the book not to go.
p: We fear no one will believe us. That we don't have the skills. That we aren't capable. But God has already told us, “*lo, I am with you alway, even unto the end of the world.*” ([[Matthew 28:20]])
p: How often are we Jonahs, running from the calling? The wicked who may seek your life cannot do anything but threaten you with Heaven.
refs: Exodus 4:10-12; Jonah 1:3; Psalm 27:1
