=== Sowing the seed of the word
# from 6136
--- The seed groweth, he knoweth not how
kicker: Sowing the seed of the word
scripture: Mark 4:26-28 | mark: the seed should spring and grow up, he knoweth not how
p: The seed is the word, Jesus tells us. God doesn't dictate to the seed that it germinate, that it sprout, when it should flower and bud, that it bear fruit. Only that it will as it will, and in due season be ready for harvest.
p: We can trace our lineage in terms of believers who led others to Christ, who led still others, who eventually were those who brought us to salvation. Like a family tree, stretching back to the seed that was sown.

# from 17539
--- Cast thy bread upon the waters
kicker: Sowing the seed of the word
big: Ecclesiastes 11:1 | mark: Cast thy bread upon the waters
p: *He that observeth the wind shall not sow; and he that regardeth the clouds shall not reap.* Sow your seed in the morning and evening and at every opportunity, and give the rest to God. Be ready at any opportunity to give the gospel.
big: Isaiah 55:11 | mark: it shall not return unto me void

# from 14599, 5649
--- The way side, and building up
kicker: Sowing the seed of the word
p: Naaman confesses there is no other God, and in the same breath asks pardon to bow in the house of Rimmon. In many ways, this is the experience many have when given the Gospel. They are like the seed sown on the pathway in the parable of the Sower ([[Matthew 13:19]]).
p: A reminder that it is not just saving souls that we should do, but then building upon that salvation, encouraging and edifying babes in Christ, as we would our own children, to walk a Christian walk.
refs: 2 Kings 5:17-19; 1 Thessalonians 2:11-12
