=== Choose ye this day
# from 14523, 14716
--- How long halt ye between two opinions?
kicker: Choose ye this day
big: 1 Kings 18:21 | mark: How long halt ye between two opinions
p: There are saved people in the world. There is a vast majority of those who are caught between, often in indecision. Soul-winning, giving the gospel to the unbelievers, forces them to make this choice. And many receive it gladly.

--- How long halt ye between two opinions?, continued
kicker: Choose ye this day
big: Joshua 24:15 | mark: choose you this day whom ye will serve
p: Our job is to go work the harvest. To make people decide if they choose life or death.

# from 14717, 15442 (church)
--- Not peace, but division
kicker: Choose ye this day
big: Luke 12:51 | mark: Nay; but rather division
p: We all have had loved ones, family, friends, who we have shared the gospel with, but we hesitate to push the issue. Sometimes, it's embarrassment at our own sins being evident to those who know us best. But often, it is the understanding that pushing the issue may push them away.
p: Christians are often so afraid that our loved ones will perish, but at the same time are scared we could be the cause of it.
refs: Matthew 10:37; Deuteronomy 30:19
read: app:doctrine-soulwinning~14523 | How long halt ye between two opinions
read: app:doctrine-soulwinning~14716 | Revival forces men to choose life or death
read: app:doctrine-soulwinning~14717 | Not peace but division

=== Go
# from 16276, 16326
--- Revival starts at the door
kicker: Go
lead: Revival doesn't start by some magical change of heart among the heathen!
p: Revival starts with a knock on the door by a saved Christian with the King James Bible in their hand and the love of God in their heart.
p: Organized door knocking is more profitable, and having a place to send the souls won to be taught all things and be baptized is crucial. If you go to church, and they don't have soul-winning, ask the pastor to start a program. Offer to organize it.

# from 7772
--- Do the first works
kicker: Go
scripture: Revelation 2:4-5 | mark: thou hast left thy first love; do the first works
p: The first love of any church is the winning of souls to Christ. The joy of our salvation when fresh leads to our telling everyone about the good news. Churches grow from giving the Gospel. But many successful churches plateau and settle in with who they have.

# from 16121, 11751
--- Don't wait for persecution
kicker: Go
scripture: Acts 8:1-4 | mark: they that were scattered abroad went every where preaching the word
p: Jesus told them to go out to the world and spread the Gospel to every creature. And instead they stayed in Jerusalem. So the Lord brought tribulation and persecution, scattering the saints abroad, so that they would preach everywhere. Are you waiting for the tribulation to go out into all the world and preach?
p: Instead of prepping for doomsday and hiding our light under a bushel in some mountainous retreat, we should be winning souls. Jeremiah isn't in the wilderness far away from the people, but in Jerusalem, the heart of darkness.

# from 16277, 18019, 14811
--- Go soul winning [title]
overline: Soul winning
heading: Go Ye Into All the World
center: If you know the love Jesus has for you, if you have felt that love, how can you not scream it from the rooftops? How can you not go out into the highways and hedges to let everyone know that Jesus loves them?
big: Mark 16:15 | mark: Go ye into all the world, and preach the gospel to every creature

--- Go soul winning, continued
center: The great commission is a command. Soul winning is an act of faith and love.
